y intermediate is nonfinite. Otherwise return $(v,\\widehat\\tau,\\widehat\\alpha,C_+)$ marked `reflector`. For a separate block $Y$, apply the stored reflector by computing its sequential column dots in increasing column order, then the vector $p_i=\\operatorname{fl}(\\widehat\\tau v_i)$ in increasing $i$, and then each rounded product and subtraction by increasing column and row; omit the target-column overwrite. Store reflector factors with their identity/reflector marker to represent the exact orthogonal product; a rounded explicit dense product is a separate output with its own arithmetic error. For a nonzero stored $v$, the associated exact reflector is $H(v)=I-2vv^T/(v^Tv)$, using [[def-householder-reflector]] and the QR convention of [[def-full-reduced-and-column-pivoted-computational-qr-factorisations]]. This definition does not assert a local backward-error bound.",
