           "source_section": "Definition",
-          "quote": "**Input:** an ODE field $f:D\\to\\mathbb R^d$ on the open domain $D\\subseteq\\mathbb R\\times\\mathbb R^d$, $(t_n,y_n)\\in D$, $h>0$, $\\gamma>0$, a finite real Jacobian matrix $\\widetilde J_n\\in\\mathbb R^{d\\times d}$, a residual tolerance $\\varepsilon\\ge0$, the selected stored finite set $\\mathbb F$ of [[def-operationwise-real-complex-floating-point-model-with-sqrt-and-fma]], a terminating field-evaluation routine and a terminating partial exact-storage check, and the terminating certified-norm routine of [[alg-rosenbrock-shifted-qr-solver-with-residual-certificate]]. For an exact real scalar, vector, or matrix $v$, `store(v)` returns $v$ if every entry belongs to $\\mathbb F$ and returns `unavailable` otherwise; it does not round. Apply it before each QR call.\n\n1. Form $M=I_d-\\gamma h\\widetilde J_n$ by exact outer arithmetic and set $M_s:=\\operatorname{store}(M)$. If storage returns `unavailable`, return $(y_n,\\texttt{representation-unavailable})$. Factor $M_s$. If factorization reports `singular-factor` or `range-failure`, return $(y_n,\\text{that status})$.\n2. Evaluate $b=f(t_n,y_n)$ exactly and set $b_s:=\\operatorname{store}(b)$. If storage returns `unavailable`, return $(y_n,\\texttt{representation-unavailable})$. Call the factor object's `solve(b_s,\\varepsilon)`. If the solve status is not `success`, return $(y_n,\\text{that status})$ and retain its residual bound for diagnosis.\n3. If the solve returns $k_n$ and a certified residual upper bound $\\rho_n\\le\\varepsilon$, return $(y_n+h k_n,\\texttt{success},\\rho_n)$.\n\nThe exact-arithmetic stage equation is $M k_n=f(t_n,y_n)$, exactly the map of [[def-rosenbrock-euler-step-map]]. Its residual $Mk_n-f(t_n,y_n)$ is the update residual of the linear stage equation in the sense of [[def-implicit-residual-and-algebraic-error-units]]. For this mixed-arithmetic specification, evaluations and outer affine combinations are exact real operations and every matrix/RHS passed to QR must pass `store`; only the factorization, triangular solve, and residual check use rounded operations. A full hardware-rounding theorem for outer operations needs additional certified evaluation and update-error terms. This implementation has one shifted-matrix factorization and one stage solve. It does not turn a small residual into a forward-error claim without an inverse bound.\n",
+          "quote": "**Input:** an ODE field $f:D\\to\\mathbb R^d$ on the open domain $D\\subseteq\\mathbb R\\times\\mathbb R^d$, $(t_n,y_n)\\in D$, $h>0$, $\\gamma>0$, a finite real Jacobian matrix $\\widetilde J_n\\in\\mathbb R^{d\\times d}$, a residual tolerance $\\varepsilon\\ge0$, a unit roundoff $u>0$ with $du<1$, the selected stored finite set $\\mathbb F$ of [[def-operationwise-real-complex-floating-point-model-with-sqrt-and-fma]], a terminating field-evaluation routine that returns either the exact value $f(t,y)$ or `evaluation-failure` for each requested $(t,y)\\in D$, a terminating partial exact-storage check `store`, and a terminating certificate evaluator `evaluator` meeting the input contract of [[alg-rosenbrock-shifted-qr-solver-with-residual-certificate]]. For an exact real scalar, vector, or matrix $v$, `store(v)` returns $v$ if every entry belongs to $\\mathbb F$ and returns `unavailable` otherwise; it does not round. Apply it before each factorization call.\n\n1. Form $M=I_d-\\gamma h\\widetilde J_n$ by exact outer arithmetic and set $M_s:=\\operatorname{store}(M)$. If storage returns `unavailable`, return $(y_n,\\texttt{representation-unavailable})$. Call `factor(M_s,u,evaluator)` of [[alg-rosenbrock-shifted-qr-solver-with-residual-certificate]]. If it returns a factorization failure status, return $(y_n,\\text{that status})$; otherwise retain the returned factor object.\n2. Request the field evaluation at $(t_n,y_n)$. If it returns `evaluation-failure`, return $(y_n,\\texttt{field-evaluation-failure})$. Otherwise set $b=f(t_n,y_n)$ to the returned exact value and set $b_s:=\\operatorname{store}(b)$. If storage returns `unavailable`, return $(y_n,\\texttt{representation-unavailable})$. Call the retained factor object's `solve(b_s,\\varepsilon)`. If the solve status is not `success`, return $(y_n,\\text{that status})$ and retain its residual bound for diagnosis.\n3. If the solve returns $k_n$ and a certified residual upper bound $\\rho_n\\le\\varepsilon$, return $(y_n+h k_n,\\texttt{success},\\rho_n)$.\n\nThe exact-arithmetic stage equation is $M k_n=f(t_n,y_n)$, exactly the map of [[def-rosenbrock-euler-step-map]]. Its residual $Mk_n-f(t_n,y_n)$ is the update residual of the linear stage equation in the sense of [[def-implicit-residual-and-algebraic-error-units]]. For this mixed-arithmetic specification, evaluations and outer affine combinations are exact real operations and every matrix/RHS passed to factorization or solve must pass `store`; only the factorization, triangular solve, and residual dot products use rounded operations, while residual-bound formation is delegated to the terminating certificate evaluator. A full hardware-rounding theorem for outer operations needs additional certified evaluation and update-error terms. This implementation has one shifted-matrix factorization and one stage solve. It does not turn a small residual into a forward-error claim without an inverse bound.",
