-          "quote": "Input a real active column $x\\in\\mathbb F^r$ and trailing block $B\\in\\mathbb F^{r\\times q}$, with entries in the floating-point system, $r\\ge1$, and $q\\ge0$. If $x=0$, return the identity action and copy $B$. Otherwise let $s=\\max_i|x_i|>0$, compute $z_i=\\operatorname{fl}(x_i/s)$ and $t=\\operatorname{fl}(\\sum_i z_i^2)$ by sequential rounded operations, then $\\widehat r=\\operatorname{fl}(s\\operatorname{fl}(\\sqrt t))$. Set $\\sigma=1$ when $x_1=0$ and $\\sigma=\\operatorname{sign}(x_1)$ otherwise, $\\widehat\\alpha=-\\sigma\\widehat r$, $v_i=\\operatorname{fl}(x_i-\\widehat\\alpha\\,1_{i=1})$, $w=\\operatorname{fl}(v^Tv)$, and $\\widehat\\tau=\\operatorname{fl}(2/w)$. Compute $d=\\operatorname{fl}(v^TB)$ by sequential rounded products and additions, $p_i=\\operatorname{fl}(\\widehat\\tau v_i)$, $U_{ij}=\\operatorname{fl}(p_i d_j)$, and $\\widehat B_{ij}=\\operatorname{fl}(B_{ij}-U_{ij})$. The complete active output is $C_+=[\\widehat\\alpha e_1\\;\\widehat B]$: write exact zeros below its first diagonal entry. This fixes the multiplication order and includes the column overwrite in the analyzed step. Return the first range failure on any invalid or out-of-range operation; return failure if $t$, $\\widehat r$, or $w$ is not positive normal, or any intermediate is nonfinite. Otherwise return $(v,\\widehat\\tau,\\widehat\\alpha,C_+)$. Store these reflectors to represent the exact orthogonal product; a rounded explicit dense product is a separate output with its own arithmetic error. The exact reflector associated with nonzero stored $v$ is $H(v)=I-2vv^T/(v^Tv)$, using [[def-householder-reflector]] and the QR convention of [[def-full-reduced-and-column-pivoted-computational-qr-factorisations]]. This definition does not assert a local backward-error bound.\n\n",
+          "quote": "Input a real active column $x\\in\\mathbb F^r$ and trailing block $B\\in\\mathbb F^{r\\times q}$ with entries in the floating-point system, $r\\ge1$, $q\\ge0$. If every component of $x$ is zero, return the identity action and a copy of $B$, with the active output column set to exact zeros, so that $C_+=[0e_1\\;B]$; return $(v=0,\\widehat\\tau=0,\\widehat\\alpha=0,C_+)$ marked `identity`. Otherwise compute $s=\\max_{1\\le i\\le r}|x_i|>0$, and then, in increasing $i$, compute $z_i=\\operatorname{fl}(x_i/s)$. Initialize $t=0$ and, in increasing $i$, compute $a_i=\\operatorname{fl}(z_i z_i)$ followed by $t=\\operatorname{fl}(t+a_i)$. Compute $h=\\operatorname{fl}(\\sqrt t)$ and then $\\widehat r=\\operatorname{fl}(s h)$. Set $\\sigma=1$ if $x_1=0$ and $\\sigma=\\operatorname{sign}(x_1)$ otherwise, and set $\\widehat\\alpha=-\\sigma\\widehat r$ using the exact sign change. Compute $v_1=\\operatorname{fl}(x_1-\\widehat\\alpha)$, then copy $v_i=x_i$ exactly for $i=2,\\ldots,r$.\n\nInitialize $w=0$ and, in increasing $i$, compute $a_i=\\operatorname{fl}(v_i v_i)$ followed by $w=\\operatorname{fl}(w+a_i)$. Then compute $\\widehat\\tau=\\operatorname{fl}(2/w)$. For each column $j=1,\\ldots,q$ in increasing order, initialize $d_j=0$ and, in increasing $i$, compute $a_{ij}=\\operatorname{fl}(v_i B_{ij})$ followed by $d_j=\\operatorname{fl}(d_j+a_{ij})$. After all $d_j$ have been computed, in increasing $i$ compute $p_i=\\operatorname{fl}(\\widehat\\tau v_i)$. Then, in increasing $j$ and within each column in increasing $i$, compute $U_{ij}=\\operatorname{fl}(p_i d_j)$ and $\\widehat B_{ij}=\\operatorname{fl}(B_{ij}-U_{ij})$ in that order. The complete active output is $C_+=[\\widehat\\alpha e_1\\;\\widehat B]$, with exact zeros written below its first diagonal entry. If any elementary operation fails, return the first range failure with its stage and indices in the order above. Also return failure if $t$, $\\widehat r$, or $w$ is not positive normal, or any intermediate is nonfinite. Otherwise return $(v,\\widehat\\tau,\\widehat\\alpha,C_+)$ marked `reflector`. For a separate block $Y$, apply the stored reflector by computing its sequential column dots in increasing column order, then the vector $p_i=\\operatorname{fl}(\\widehat\\tau v_i)$ in increasing $i$, and then each rounded product and subtraction by increasing column and row; omit the target-column overwrite. Store reflector factors with their identity/reflector marker to represent the exact orthogonal product; a rounded explicit dense product is a separate output with its own arithmetic error. For a nonzero stored $v$, the associated exact reflector is $H(v)=I-2vv^T/(v^Tv)$, using [[def-householder-reflector]] and the QR convention of [[def-full-reduced-and-column-pivoted-computational-qr-factorisations]]. This definition does not assert a local backward-error bound.",
