+          "claim": "Write $f=f(t,y)$, $f_t=\\partial_tf(t,y)$, and $J=D_yf(t,y)$. From $M^{-1}-I=\\gamma hM^{-1}W$ and the uniform inverse bound, $\\|M^{-1}-I\\|\\le\\gamma hBW_0$. Thus [F1] gives $k_1=f+\\gamma h(Wf+f_t)+r_1$ with $\\|r_1\\|\\le C_1h^2$, where $C_1=\\gamma^2BW_0(W_0F+F_t)$.",
