+          "claim": "Taylor's formula [F2] along the segment $(t+s,y+s k_1)$ gives $f(t+h,y+hk_1)=f+h f_t+hJf+R$, with $\\|R\\|\\le h^2\\{\\frac H2(1+K_1)^2+L C_k\\}$, where $K_1:=B(F+\\gamma h_0F_t)$ bounds $\\|k_1\\|$ and $C_k:=\\gamma B(W_0F+F_t)$ bounds $\\|k_1-f\\|/h$. Substitution in the second equation of [F1] yields $Mk_2=-f+h\\{Jf+(1-3\\gamma)f_t-2\\gamma Wf\\}+E$ with $\\|E\\|\\le h^2(C_f+2C_1)$, where $C_f:=\\frac H2(1+K_1)^2+LC_k$.",
